{
  "$schema_note": "Install-manifest serialization test fixtures (Rust). Each `cases[]` entry's fields describe a Manifest value; expected.serialized is the byte-identical JSON text the Rust manifest writer must produce for it (schema_version, strategy, installed_at, destination, source, status, files -- files always rendered sorted by path, 2-space indent, trailing newline, no ASCII-escaping of non-ASCII text). `destination` is the install ROOT relative to target_dir (always \".\" -- installs span two roots under target_dir: \".kiro/\" for agents and context, \".konductor/\" for skills, since skills live outside \".kiro/skills/\" for per-agent scoping); each files[].path is relative to `destination` and carries its own content-type prefix, e.g. \".kiro/agents/k-example.json\" or \".konductor/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\". `source` is the absolute `--from <repo-root>` path this install run was given, or `null` when none was recorded (rendered explicitly as JSON `null`, never omitted, mirroring `files[].sha256`'s own null-not-omitted convention -- see manifest.rs's `Manifest` doc comment). `status` is either \"in_progress\" (the write-ahead record, written before any file is copied) or \"complete\" (written after every file has actually been copied). `files[].sha256` is `null` in an \"in_progress\" record (the real content, and therefore its hash, does not exist yet) and a 64-char lowercase-hex string once `status` is \"complete\". `files[].provenance` is one of \"created\" (nothing was at this path before), \"replaced_ours\" (a prior Konductor install owned this exact path), or \"replaced_foreign\" (pre-existing content this install did not create, now overwritten -- a future uninstall must never delete this path). `error_cases[]` entries describe an on-disk `.konductor/manifest` (raw_json) that read_manifest must reject; expected.reason_substring is a literal substring the error message must contain -- checked by content, not just exit behavior. SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 -- JSON has no native comment syntax; this $schema_note field carries the required license header.",
